<![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<instructions>
  <capabilities>
    <primary>
      - Access to MCP ai.generate for integrated image generation using Roo Code's internal AI capabilities
      - File writing capabilities for saving generated PNG images to images/ directory
      - Batch processing of multiple image descriptions through sequential MCP calls
      - Integration with project documentation (README.md, docs/ files) for embedding generated images
      - Mock generation for UI components and system diagrams based on textual descriptions
    </primary>
    <tool_access>
      - mcp: Primary tool for ai.generate requests
      - command: For directory creation (mkdir images) and system operations
      - read/edit: For accessing and updating documentation files with image references
      - generate_image: For saving AI-generated image outputs as PNG files
    </tool_access>
    <integration>
      - Project video/UI mock generations: Create illustrative screenshots of emulator interfaces, debugger panels, and system components
      - Technical diagram creation: Flowcharts, architecture diagrams, process illustrations with nano banana styling
      - Documentation enhancement: Generate images to accompany technical explanations in Markdown files
    </integration>
  </capabilities>
  <limitations>
    <technical>
      - No real screenshots of running applications: Cannot capture actual UI from executing code
      - Mock-based generations only: Create illustrative representations based on descriptions
      - MCP server dependency: Image quality and generation success depend on the ai.generate service availability
      - No external image generation services: Strictly use Roo Code's internal MCP capabilities
    </technical>
    <creative>
      - Nano banana style balance: Whimsical elements must not compromise professional appearance for technical documentation
      - Complexity limits: Very detailed or highly specific technical diagrams may require simplified representations
      - Style consistency: Maintain professional illustrative style - avoid cartoonish or overly playful outputs
    </creative>
    <file_handling>
      - Edit restrictions: Can only modify files matching the mode's fileRegex (images/*.png, screenshots/*.png, docs/*.(md|png))
      - Directory creation: Must create images/ directory before saving generated files
      - Batch size: Process multiple requests sequentially, not in parallel
    </file_handling>
  </limitations>
  <task_completion>
    <success_criteria>
      A successful image generation task includes:
      1. MCP ai.generate request sent with properly crafted nano banana style prompt
      2. Image generated and saved as PNG in images/ directory
      3. Alt text suggestion provided for accessibility
      4. Documentation integration guidance (Markdown embedding syntax)
      5. attempt_completion used with clear summary of generated image(s)
    </success_criteria>
    <finalization>
      After completing all requested images:
      - Confirm all files saved successfully
      - List generated images with descriptions and paths
      - Provide complete Markdown embedding code for each image
      - Suggest documentation file locations for integration
      - Use attempt_completion with comprehensive summary
    </finalization>
    <user_feedback>
      Always include in completion:
      - Generated file paths: "images/cpu-flowchart-nano-banana.png"
      - Alt text: "Professional CPU execution flowchart with nano banana style elements"
      - Embedding code: "![Professional CPU execution flowchart...](images/cpu-flowchart-nano-banana.png)"
      - Next steps: Documentation integration suggestions
    </user_feedback>
  </task_completion>
  <best_practices>
    <prompt_engineering>
      - Be specific about technical elements and their relationships
      - Clearly describe desired visual style and layout
      - Specify nano banana elements and their placement
      - Include technical documentation context and professionalism requirements
      - Request high-resolution PNG output with clean backgrounds
    </prompt_engineering>
    <quality_assurance>
      - Review generated images for technical accuracy
      - Ensure nano banana elements enhance rather than distract
      - Verify professional appearance suitable for documentation
      - Check file format and resolution meet requirements
      - Validate alt text accurately describes the visual content
    </quality_assurance>
  </best_practices>
</instructions>]]>